Shares the BMDS desktop with VNC viewers: TigerVNC, TurboVNC, Remmina, noVNC, RealVNC.

Flat parts of the screen and text go losslessly (fills, palettes, zlib); pictures, video and
games go through the board's hardware JPEG encoder; viewers draw the pointer themselves, so it
moves without delay. Keys, the mouse, the wheel and the clipboard come back; copies go both ways,
in full UTF-8 with viewers that have the Extended Clipboard (TigerVNC), as Latin-1 with the rest.
Up to four viewers at once: the first in has the keyboard and mouse, the rest watch; the tray's
Give Input To moves it.

It listens on the board's own loopback: reach it through SSH,
    ssh -L 5900:localhost:5900 board
then point a viewer at localhost:5900. Set a password with 'vncserver passwd'. With the setting
vnc/listen at lan (and a password) it listens on the network too, with TLS (VeNCrypt) and the
board's own certificate: 'tls cert' shows the fingerprint a viewer asks you to accept. Viewers
without VeNCrypt (TightVNC) need vnc/encryption at none: the password alone, readable on the wire.
Start it from the launcher (VNC Server), or with 'vncserver' (from autoexec.sh, or over SSH);
Stop Server in its tray icon's menu or 'vncserver stop' ends it. While it runs it has an icon in
the tray (a red dot on it while a viewer is in), and a viewer coming or going shows a notification.

Needs BMDS 0.4.0 or newer.
